-- title:
--   Two-branch normalisation at the node j=0: width divides the Fricke exponent
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and let $\mathrm{red}:A\to k$ be a ring homomorphism whose zero set is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$. Assume $0\in k$ lies in `ssJSet q k`, that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $0$ has no point $P$ with $q\cdot P=0$ other than $P=0$. Let $f\ne 0$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$. Suppose that for every place $W$ of this field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (a proper valuation subring containing the constants and a principal ideal ring), with $\mathrm{ord}$ the associated normalised additive valuation, the following holds: if there are $x,y\in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,x=0$, $\mathrm{red}\,y=0^q$, $W.\mathrm{ord}(j-x)>0$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j_q-y)>0$, where $j$ is the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` and $j_q$ that of `qExpand ℚ (1 * q) jq`, then $W.\mathrm{ord}(f)=0$. Then there are $c\in\overline{\mathbb Q}^{\times}$ and $m\in\mathbb Z$ with $\mathrm{jWidth}(0)=3$ dividing $m$ such that the Laurent series of $c\cdot f$ and that of the Fricke involute `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)` of $(c\,q^{m})\cdot f$ both lie in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the subring generated by constants from $A$ together with the series $j$ and $j_q$ at the prime of elements of zero reduction, and both have nonzero image under the reduction homomorphism `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom (1 * q) A.toSubring red` into $k((t))$.
--
--   This is the two-branch normalisation at the supersingular node with $j$-invariant $0$ on the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(q)$: a function with no zeros or poles in the tube around that node can be scaled to have nonzero reduction on each of the two branches, and the power of $q$ relating the two scalings is divisible by the width $3$ of the node. It strengthens the one-branch statement [`ModularCurve.CharPReduction.exists_smul_mem_modularLocalized_and_modularRedLocHom_ne_zero_of_charP`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPReduction.exists_smul_mem_modularLocalized_and_modularRedLocHom_ne_zero_of_charP) and is used by [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_int_mul_pow_param_isUnit_of_forall_centred_zero_ord_eq_zero_of_crossingPresentation`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_int_mul_pow_param_isUnit_of_forall_centred_zero_ord_eq_zero_of_crossingPresentation).
